  "description": "Not a published list: built so the sweeps reach Kabonesa Wu: Netspace Thrillseeker, Kitara's Shaper identity, whose click searches the stack for a non-virus program and installs it 1[credit] cheaper, removing it from the game if it is still installed when the turn ends. On Level Pegging's list, its identity swapped; named to sort after every other deck, so the sweep schedule of those before it does not move. Kitara Stage 12f: two Compile for two Rejig, a run that installs a program from the stack or heap for nothing at its first encounter; Level Pegging keeps Rejig Kitara Stage 15: two Flame-out for its two Tinkering, a host whose credits pay for the program on it.",
